{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the heavens were completed, etc.</b> This verse — we do not know what it comes to teach us. It appears to intend, after the manner of the Sages of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 68:9), that the Holy One, blessed be He, is the place of the world. We also find that He fills the world, as stated (Isaiah 6:3): ״מְלֹא כָל הָאָרֶץ כְּבוֹדוֹ״. From this it follows that His light, blessed be He, is found surrounding the world and within its interior. One must set the mind to know the reason of the matter — why HaShem did so. I have it on tradition from the mouths of elders of Torah that the reason HaShem made the world spherical is so that it would stand and endure through the equalization of the forces of its parts. The explanation of the matter is this: you must know that there is no yearning in the world so sweet, so beloved, so desirable, so cherished, so longed for, and so hoped for by the creations — particularly by the parts of the spiritual [domain] that recognize and know the aspect of the light of the Godhead, such as attachment to His light, blessed be He. Toward Him every vital soul longs, that reaches to know some of the pleasantness of His light, blessed be He; their soul goes out to gaze upon the pleasantness of HaShem. And you must know that everything HaShem created in His world, HaShem formed within it an aspect of intellection and discernment according to its level — speaking creatures and non-speaking creatures, plants and inanimate matter — each has a power of intellection to recognize its Creator according to its grasp. Through this you will gain understanding to know in what thing the standing of the world depends, and that it stands without swaying, for HaShem has revealed His secret to those who fear Him, and through the medium of the remarks made above, the perceptible has been grasped. It is that through the medium of His sweet and hoped-for light that surrounds the sphericity of the world in equilibrium, every part of the surrounding [surface] of the world intensifies with the power of the fire of yearning that burns within it to draw near to the aspect of the totality of the hoped-for source. And since every aspect of the world's surrounding has an equal measure of yearning within it — both from the side of what emanates from them, for the desire of one part is not greater than that of another, for were this so, through this medium the intensification of that part would increase and its counterpart would weaken; and both from the side of that toward which [it turns], namely the pleasant light, for it is not closer to one part of the surrounding than to another, for were this so, one part of the world would grow through the power of its intensification more than another part — rather, all is in equilibrium. And every hair's-breadth thread of every part of the surrounding [surface] of the world intensifies to draw near and pulls toward the direction facing it; and through the medium of the intensification drawn from every side of the sphericity of the world, the world is found standing and enduring, each part holding up its fellow through the aforesaid medium. Thus the entire world is fastened with pegs and nails of the desire of the Creator toward aspects of spiritual longing and inclination that are within it to draw near to the Sweet One, may His name be exalted. Through this you grasp the reason HaShem created the world spherical — and understand it. Through this too we have found the reason why the world is fixed and planted without swaying, for swaying would come about through the predominance or weakening of one part over the parts that hold it up, whereas in this reality it is impossible to sway in any manner." "<b>And it is possible</b> that to this the Sages, may their memory be blessed, alluded in the pleasantness of their words (Ḥagigah 12b), and this is their language: ״They stand but do not know on what they stand,״ end of quote. The intention is that if the creations possessed this discernment, and knew the exalted height of the holy love and the yearning of the creations toward the hidden Sweet One, and saw how great is the intensity of the hope and the intensification of this inanimate thing — which is the world — that intensifies to draw near to enjoy the hoped-for light, and no laxity occurred in any part of the world's surrounding — they would draw an a fortiori conclusion from this: how much more must man act, for in him the discernment and intellection were multiplied. You must also know that since all creations fill the world — everything in which the vital spirit exists — the Sages, may their memory be blessed (Yalkut Tehillim 150), said that no soul settles in its place except by virtue of the fact that there exists for it something to long for and hope for, [namely] the fullness of this world; without this the soul would abhor the flesh. For this reason HaShem illuminated His world with His glory, and His glory fills the world; thus the world is found within the very within of its Creator, and the light of the Creator within all the world and surrounding His world. Through this the world stood and endured, through the medium of yearning toward the Existent One — and this is what the verse says: <b>and the heavens and the earth and all their host were completed</b>. The meaning of ״וַיְכֻלּוּ״ is after the manner of the verse (Psalms 84:3): ״נִכְסְפָה וְגַם כָּלְתָה״ (my soul longs and even pines). Through this medium the creation was completed and established. And the reason the verse expressed the matter in this language, ״וַיְכֻלּוּ״, is to allude that it is a great yearning, to the point of the part's being consumed with longing (כְּלוֹת) toward the Whole — and this is a level greater than the level of desire and yearning. This is what David alluded in saying ״נִכְסְפָה וְגַם כָּלְתָה״ — this declares that this level is greater than the level preceding it, and through the medium of this level and its intensification the world endures. This is the secret of the appellation ״חַי הָעוֹלָמִים״ (Life of the Worlds) — and understand it. And it is the secret of ״בְּאוֹר פְּנֵי מֶלֶךְ חַיִּים״ (Proverbs 16:15, in the light of the King's face is life)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:32.665223703Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}